<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Rheged</h1><p class="st-meta">500 CE – 638 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A British kingdom of the 'Old North' around the Solway, celebrated in Welsh poetry for King Urien and his battles against the Angles.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Rheged emerged in the 6th century among the Brittonic kingdoms of northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>. Its location is uncertain, but scholars usually place it around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlisle">Carlisle</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumbria">Cumbria</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-galloway">Galloway</a>. Its fame rests on poems attributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taliesin">Taliesin</a> praising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urien-rheged">Urien Rheged</a>, and on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/historia-brittonum">Historia Brittonum</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urien-rheged">Urien</a> is remembered as a leader of a coalition of British kings that besieged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angles">Angles</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-bernicia">Bernicia</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lindisfarne">Lindisfarne</a> in the late 6th century, before he was murdered by a rival. Welsh tradition remembers the court as a centre of bardic patronage. Its society and economy are otherwise almost unknown.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Rheged seems to have passed peacefully to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-northumbria">Northumbria</a>, perhaps through the marriage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiu">Oswiu</a> to Rhiainfellt, a descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urien-rheged">Urien</a>, around 638. Its memory lived on in Welsh poetry and Arthurian romance, where Urien and his son Owain became famous figures.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-rheged.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Rheged" width="320" height="277"><figcaption>Image: Pickled Pigeon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hen_Ogledd_Map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 CE – 638 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Urien Rheged, Owain ab Urien</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Cumbric</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rheged</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=569&amp;focus=kingdom-of-rheged" aria-label="Kingdom of Rheged on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4616 300 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Rheged lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4936 556L4945 553"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4945 553h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4936 556h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4936 556h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=569&amp;focus=kingdom-of-rheged">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
